    # The user's own words, the mechanics, the constitution row that reaches every
    # generated org, and the guard that blocks the shape. Four paths, four breaks.
    ("finish-not-hedge: the user's words are retained verbatim in the directive block",
     SKL, "del", "always prefer finishing rather than hedging"),
    # ── the measured length ceiling (2026-09-07) ─────────────────────────────
    # Breaking either SIDE of the comparison must fire it: the constant in the script
    # and the sentence in doctrine that retires the old number.
    ("length ceiling: wf-conform's constant equals the measured floor doctrine states",
     CNFM, "del", "DEFAULT_LENGTH_CEILING = 172"),
    # ── the six audit-found defects (2026-09-08) ─────────────────────────────
    # Reported by a live `/workforce audit` on another project, each verified against
    # this tree. Every one of them was GREEN under a presence check while being wrong,
    # which is the pattern the whole block exists to break: a detector that asks whether
    # a string landed cannot tell you whether what landed can be RUN.
    ("platform: MEASURED carries the conditions it was measured under",
     "workforce/references/platform.md", "del", "AND MAY NOT BE APPLIED OUTSIDE"),
    ("platform: fact 23b records that single-hit self-identification does not generalise",
     "workforce/references/platform.md", "del", "WAS MEASURED WITH ONE AGENT IN THE SESSION"),
    ("org: a returned HANDOFF has a consumer, and it spawns rather than re-dispatches",
     "workforce/references/procedures/org.md", "del",
     "A returned `HANDOFF` means SPAWN A SUCCESSOR"),
    ("conform: a node that reports to itself is named as that, not as a missing edge",
