    ("checkrun: a command wired into `## Guardrails` is resolved, not just counted present",
     CKR, "del", "def check_guardrails"),
    # DELETE WHAT THE ASSERTION TESTS, NOT A LONGER STRING CONTAINING IT. The check
    # reads `"BARE_WF_RX" in _c6`; removing only the definition line left every other
    # mention in the file, so the substring survived and this case reported VACUOUS
    # while the mutation landed. `delall` on the tested substring is the mutation the
    # assertion actually describes.
    ("checkrun: a command wired into `## Guardrails` is resolved, not just counted present",
     CKR, "delall", "BARE_WF_RX"),
    ("checkrun: only the row with a certain fix blocks; naming a command is not running it",
